---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for DailyDialz — how Dimension Seven Systems accesses, uses, stores, and discloses information when you use DailyDialz."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  hideNav
>
  <section class="bg-bg px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <article class="prose-legal mx-auto max-w-[760px]">
      <h1 class="text-[40px] font-bold text-text sm:text-[48px]">DailyDialz Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-muted">Effective Date: August 8, 2026</p>

      <p>
        DailyDialz is a product of <strong class="font-semibold text-text">Dimension Seven Systems</strong>
        ("Dimension Seven Systems," "DailyDialz," "we," "us" or "our").
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how information is accessed, used, stored and disclosed when you use the DailyDialz
        application, website and related services.
      </p>
      <p>
        DailyDialz is designed to help users work through calling lists using their existing mobile phone. We believe a
        calling tool should have access only to the information it actually needs to perform that job.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information DailyDialz May Access</h2>
      <p>Depending on the features you use, DailyDialz may access the following information.</p>

      <h3>Account Information</h3>
      <p>If you sign in or activate a DailyDialz license, we may process information such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
        <li>License or activation information</li>
        <li>Information necessary to verify your access to DailyDialz</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Google Account and Google Sheets Data</h3>
      <p>
        If you connect DailyDialz to your Google account, DailyDialz may request permission to access Google Drive files
        that you specifically select or authorize for use with the application.
      </p>
      <p>This may include Google Sheets containing:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Names</li>
        <li>Phone numbers</li>
        <li>Company names</li>
        <li>Email addresses</li>
        <li>Lead information</li>
        <li>Notes</li>
        <li>Custom spreadsheet fields</li>
        <li>Call outcomes or dispositions</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        DailyDialz does not request unrestricted access to all files in your Google Drive simply because you connect your
        Google account.
      </p>
      <p>
        Access is intended to be limited to files you select, create or authorize for use with DailyDialz.
      </p>

      <h3>Calling and Session Information</h3>
      <p>
        When you use DailyDialz to work through a call list, the application may process information necessary to maintain
        your calling session, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The contact currently being displayed</li>
        <li>Your position in a calling queue</li>
        <li>Call dispositions</li>
        <li>Notes you enter</li>
        <li>Session status</li>
        <li>Call completion status</li>
        <li>Information required to resume an interrupted session</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        DailyDialz may write information such as dispositions, notes and call results back to a Google Sheet when you
        instruct the application to do so.
      </p>

      <h3>Device Information</h3>
      <p>
        DailyDialz may access limited information about your device when necessary to operate, troubleshoot or license the
        application.
      </p>
      <p>This may include information such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Device type</li>
        <li>Operating system version</li>
        <li>Application version</li>
        <li>Technical identifiers necessary for licensing or security</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If we later introduce optional analytics, crash reporting or similar services, this Privacy Policy will be updated
        to identify those services and the information they collect.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How DailyDialz Uses Information</h2>
      <p>Information accessed through DailyDialz is used to provide and maintain the functionality you request.</p>
      <p>This may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Loading your selected call list</li>
        <li>Displaying information about the current lead</li>
        <li>Initiating calls through your mobile device</li>
        <li>Maintaining your position in a calling session</li>
        <li>Recording dispositions and notes</li>
        <li>Writing call results to an authorized Google Sheet</li>
        <li>Resuming interrupted sessions</li>
        <li>Activating or verifying a DailyDialz license</li>
        <li>Providing customer support</li>
        <li>Protecting DailyDialz against fraud, abuse and unauthorized access</li>
        <li>Diagnosing technical problems</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use the contacts in your calling lists to market DailyDialz to those contacts.</p>
      <p>Your prospects are your prospects, not ours.</p>

      <h2>3. Google User Data</h2>
      <p>DailyDialz may use Google APIs to allow you to select and work with Google Sheets.</p>
      <p>Google account access is used only to provide the DailyDialz functionality that you authorize.</p>
      <p>DailyDialz does not use Google user data for advertising.</p>
      <p>DailyDialz does not sell Google user data.</p>
      <p>
        DailyDialz does not use information contained in your Google Sheets to build advertising profiles or independently
        market products or services to the people listed in those Sheets.
      </p>
      <p>
        Access to Google user data is limited to what is reasonably necessary to provide the features you request.
      </p>
      <p>Your use of Google services is also subject to Google's applicable terms and privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>4. Your Lead Lists</h2>
      <p>DailyDialz is designed to process lead information for you, not to acquire ownership of it.</p>
      <p>
        You retain responsibility for the lists, contacts and other information you choose to use with DailyDialz.
      </p>
      <p>Dimension Seven Systems does not claim ownership of your lead lists.</p>
      <p>We do not sell your lead lists.</p>
      <p>We do not rent your lead lists.</p>
      <p>We do not use the people contained in your lead lists as our own marketing database.</p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for ensuring that your collection, possession and use of calling-list information complies with
        applicable privacy, telemarketing, consent, Do Not Call and other laws.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
      <p>DailyDialz may store information locally on your device when necessary to operate the application.</p>
      <p>
        This may include session state, application preferences, selected fields, queue position, dispositions, notes and
        other information required to provide or resume your calling workflow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Removing the application may remove locally stored DailyDialz information. Information that has already been written
        to a Google Sheet or another service you control will remain subject to that service and your own account settings.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Information Stored by Google</h2>
      <p>
        When you use Google Sheets with DailyDialz, your spreadsheet data remains subject to your Google account and Google's
        storage systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        DailyDialz may read information from or write information to Sheets that you authorize for use with the application.
      </p>
      <p>
        Disconnecting DailyDialz does not automatically delete information already contained in your Google Drive or Google
        Sheets.
      </p>
      <p>You can manage or delete those files through your Google account.</p>

      <h2>7. Payments</h2>
      <p>Purchases may be processed by a third-party payment processor.</p>
      <p>
        When payment processing is handled by a third party, that provider may collect payment information such as your card
        number, billing information and transaction details under its own privacy policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dimension Seven Systems does not need to receive your complete payment-card number when payment information is
        collected directly by the payment processor.
      </p>
      <p>The payment processor actually used by DailyDialz will be identified during checkout.</p>

      <h2>8. How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>Dimension Seven Systems does not sell your personal information or lead-list data.</p>
      <p>
        We may disclose limited information to service providers when reasonably necessary to operate DailyDialz, such as
        providers involved in:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Payment processing</li>
        <li>Application hosting</li>
        <li>Licensing</li>
        <li>Authentication</li>
        <li>Customer support</li>
        <li>Email delivery</li>
        <li>Security</li>
        <li>Technical infrastructure</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers may process information only as necessary to perform the services for which they are engaged, subject
        to their applicable agreements and privacy practices.
      </p>
      <p>We may also disclose information when reasonably necessary to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Comply with applicable law, regulation, court order or legal process</li>
        <li>Respond to valid governmental requests</li>
        <li>Investigate fraud or abuse</li>
        <li>Protect the security of DailyDialz</li>
        <li>Protect the rights, property or safety of Dimension Seven Systems, our users or others</li>
        <li>
          Complete a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization or sale of all or part of the business, subject to
          applicable law
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. We Do Not Sell Your Data</h2>
      <p>Dimension Seven Systems does not sell your personal information.</p>
      <p>We do not sell your Google account information.</p>
      <p>We do not sell your calling lists.</p>
      <p>We do not sell information about the contacts contained in your calling lists.</p>
      <p>We do not operate DailyDialz as an advertising-data business.</p>

      <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, including
        providing DailyDialz, maintaining licenses, preventing fraud, providing support and complying with legal or
        accounting requirements.
      </p>
      <p>Different categories of information may have different retention periods.</p>
      <p>
        Information stored in your own Google account remains under your control and may be retained until you delete it
        through Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information stored locally by DailyDialz may remain until it is deleted by the application, you clear the
        application's data or you uninstall the application.
      </p>
      <p>
        As DailyDialz's licensing and server infrastructure develops, more specific retention periods may be added to this
        policy.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect information processed
        by DailyDialz.
      </p>
      <p>However, no application, device, network or electronic storage system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
      <p>
        You are also responsible for protecting your mobile device, Google account and other accounts you connect to
        DailyDialz.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        DailyDialz may request Android or Google permissions necessary to perform features you choose to use.
      </p>
      <p>Depending on the version and functionality of the application, these permissions may include access necessary to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Initiate telephone calls</li>
        <li>Connect to your Google account</li>
        <li>Select authorized Google Drive or Google Sheets files</li>
        <li>Read information from an authorized Sheet</li>
        <li>Write results to an authorized Sheet</li>
        <li>Maintain application functionality</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We attempt to request only permissions reasonably necessary for DailyDialz to perform its intended functions.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Revoking Google Access</h2>
      <p>
        You may revoke DailyDialz's access to your Google account through your Google account's security and connected-app
        settings.
      </p>
      <p>Revoking access may prevent features that depend on Google Sheets from functioning.</p>
      <p>Revoking access does not automatically delete information already contained in Google Sheets that you own.</p>

      <h2>14. Your Privacy Choices</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, applicable law may provide rights concerning your personal information.
      </p>
      <p>These rights may include the ability to request:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access to personal information we maintain about you</li>
        <li>Correction of inaccurate personal information</li>
        <li>Deletion of certain personal information</li>
        <li>Information about how your personal information is used</li>
        <li>Information about categories of third parties to which information is disclosed</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To make a privacy request, contact us using the information below.</p>
      <p>We may need to verify your identity before processing certain requests.</p>

      <h2>15. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        DailyDialz is a business productivity and sales tool and is not designed or intended for children under 13.
      </p>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13 through DailyDialz.</p>
      <p>
        If we learn that personal information from a child under 13 has been collected through DailyDialz in circumstances
        requiring deletion, we will take reasonable steps to delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        DailyDialz may interact with services operated by other companies, including Google, mobile carriers and payment
        providers.
      </p>
      <p>Those companies operate under their own terms, policies and privacy practices.</p>
      <p>Dimension Seven Systems does not control the privacy practices of independent third-party services.</p>

      <h2>17. Business Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        If Dimension Seven Systems or DailyDialz is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, bankruptcy,
        sale of assets or similar transaction, information associated with DailyDialz may be transferred as part of that
        transaction where permitted by law.
      </p>
      <p>Any successor receiving that information would remain subject to applicable privacy obligations.</p>

      <h2>18. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>DailyDialz will continue to evolve.</p>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when our product, technology, vendors, legal requirements or data practices change.
      </p>
      <p>
        When we make material changes, we will update the effective date above and may provide additional notice when
        appropriate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your continued use of DailyDialz after an updated Privacy Policy becomes effective is subject to the revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>19. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>DailyDialz is operated by:</p>
      <p>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-text">Dimension Seven Systems</strong><br />
        DailyDialz
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy questions or requests may be sent to:{" "}
        <a class="text-text underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
          >{site.email}</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Website:{" "}
        <a class="text-text underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent" href={site.url}>{site.url}</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
